{{see also|Michigan's 2nd congressional district}}

The 2nd district runs along the eastern shoreline of [[Lake Michigan]] from [[Manistee, Michigan|Manistee]] to northern [[Muskegon County, Michigan|Muskegon County]], includes parts of the [[Grand Rapids, Michigan|Grand Rapids]] suburbs in [[Kent County, Michigan|Kent]] county, and parts of [[Central Michigan]], including [[Mount Pleasant, Michigan|Mount Pleasant]] and western [[Midland County, Michigan|Midland County]]. Due to redistricting, the incumbent was Republican [[John Moolenaar]] of the [[Michigan's 4th congressional district|4th congressional district]], who was re-elected with 65.0% of the vote in 2020.<ref name=":0"/> The winner was John Moolenaar.

