{{see also|Michigan's 4th congressional district}}

The 4th district is based in southwestern Michigan, and includes the cities of [[Kalamazoo, Michigan|Kalamazoo]] and [[Holland, Michigan|Holland]]. Due to redistricting, there were two incumbents in this district – Republican [[Bill Huizenga]] of the [[Michigan's 2nd congressional district|2nd congressional district]], who was re-elected with 59.2% of the vote in 2020,<ref name=":0"/> and Republican [[Fred Upton]] of the [[Michigan's 6th congressional district|6th congressional district]], who was re-elected with 55.8% of the vote in 2020.<ref name=":0"/> Upton announced that he would be retiring at the end of his term.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.freep.com/story/news/politics/2022/04/05/representative-fred-upton-retirement/9468833002/ | title=Rep. Fred Upton announces retirement from Congress, has been in US House since 1987 }}</ref> The winner was Bill Huizenga.

