{{see also|Michigan's 11th congressional district}}

The 11th district is based solely in [[Oakland County, Michigan|Oakland County]] and includes the cities of [[Royal Oak, Michigan|Royal Oak]] and [[Pontiac, Michigan|Pontiac]]. Due to redistricting, there were two incumbents in this district – Democrat [[Haley Stevens]], who was re-elected with 50.2% of the vote in 2020,<ref name=":0"/> and Democrat [[Andy Levin]] of the [[Michigan's 9th congressional district|9th congressional district]], who was re-elected with 57.7% of the vote in 2020.<ref name=":0"/> The winner was Haley Stevens.

